# Data artifacts are verified by SHA-256 (frozen golden sets, the bake-off tasks, manifests): keep them LF on every
# checkout, whatever core.autocrlf says (owner decision 2026-10-10; a CRLF checkout broke the frozen golden hashes).
*.json    text eol=lf
*.jsonl   text eol=lf
*.csv     text eol=lf
# Files run on the Linux deployment hosts (ADR-071): a CRLF checkout would break bash and Caddy
*.sh      text eol=lf
deploy/Caddyfile text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
# The web app is checked byte for byte against LF (prettier `endOfLine: "lf"`, the regenerated Orval client in
# `npm run check`): a CRLF checkout fails both on Windows only (2026-11-21)
web/** text=auto eol=lf
*.parquet binary
*.npz     binary
*.onnx    binary
